    "agent_last_message": "The tool is built and works as specified. `node main.js --input <file> --output <file>` runs from anywhere, and the entry point is `output/main.js`. It uses only the Node standard library and has no `package.json` or `node_modules`.\n\n**Testing**\n- **Shipped tests:** the 34 tests in `output/test/` pass. Run them with `cd output && node --test`.\n- **Independent oracle:** results match a separate Python implementation I wrote from the spec on 800 random Unicode-heavy files. They also match on a 200 MB corpus and two ~46 MB multi-chunk corpora.\n- **Mutation checks:** I injected about 30 realistic bugs. All were caught except one that behaves identically to the original and one that would need an impractical hash collision.\n- **Bugs found:** the checks turned up two gaps in my own tests, which I fixed.\n- **Slow pipe case:** the read loop took 30 s on a 64 MiB word with no spaces arriving through a pipe. It now takes 0.77 s.\n\n**Speed:** about 170 MB/s on typical text (200 MB in about 1.3 s), and about 65 MB/s with a million distinct words. A simple string-and-`Map` version managed about 10 MB/s. Peak memory was 53\u2013165 MiB on 200 MB inputs, whatever the file size.\n\n**Where the spec is silent, I chose:**\n- **Malformed input:** a file that isn't valid UTF-8 exits 1 with no output. Binary data and Latin-1 text are rejected this way; NUL bytes and BOMs are valid and count normally.\n- **Lowercasing:** this is Unicode-aware, so `\u00c9COLE` and `\u00e9cole` are the same word. If you wanted ASCII-only, that is a small change.\n- **Ties:** these sort by code-point order (UTF-8 byte order), not JavaScript's default string order.\n- **Output path errors:** a bad output path (missing directory, a directory, no permission) exits 1. A disk-full error exits 2.\n- **Same file:** the tool refuses to overwrite its own input file.\n- **Arguments:** `--flag=value` works. A repeated flag, a stray positional argument, or `--help` all exit 1.\n\n**Known limit:** I can't turn V8's hard out-of-memory abort or th",
